pt09 adversarial lane, surfaces: intake normalization; zero-width and format
characters. Greens both REDs frozen in the previous commit.

1. `decodeEntities` now carries a named table instead of six names: the
   typographic set `tools/extract-source-text.mjs` already required to read
   the corpus at all, the names measured surviving extraction across the
   archived raw HTML (&raquo;, &laquo;, &copy;, &larr;, &rarr;), and the
   Latin-1 letters that any article carrying a European name contains. The
   lookup tries the exact case before folding, because `&Prime;`, `&Dagger;`
   and every Latin-1 capital differ from their lower-case twin by nothing
   else; the fold is kept so `&AMP;`-style shouting still works.

   What this cost before: 89 named entities survived extraction in the Node
   path across 13 archived sources and zero survived in the browser, so the
   Lab and its own measuring instrument read different text. `doesn&rsquo;t`
   is the expensive one — undecoded it tokenizes to doesn/rsquo/t, so the
   passage stops containing the contradiction cue `doesn't` and an entity name
   enters the token stream as a word.

2. `cleanControlCharacters` now also removes the Unicode format characters:
   soft hyphen, zero-width space, word joiner and the invisible-operator
   block, a BOM anywhere rather than only at position 0, and the bidi
   embedding and isolate controls. Every one of them splits a word for a token
   regex of `[\p{L}\p{N}]+`. All four of soft-hyphen, ZWSP, word-joiner and
   mid-text BOM now score hypergamy at 0.747, the clean value; before they
   scored 0.478, 0.562, 0.562 and 0.562, silently, with nothing in the output
   naming the cause. U+2028/U+2029 are excluded on purpose (they are line
   breaks) and so are ZWNJ/ZWJ (orthographic in Persian and Indic scripts,
   structural in emoji sequences) — the Latin-word case for those two is
   recorded as a residual rather than paid for with someone else's spelling.

Floors unmoved: 191 cases, domainRecall 1.0000, ignorePrecision 1.0000,
junkRecall 0.8529, every verdict byte-identical. Corpus stance census: 0 of
1,298 matches move — the archived corpus holds no format character and no
undecoded entity in its extracted text, which is why neither instrument could
see either class.

All 18 suite steps green.

